  "subtitle-win": [
    "France, Spain, and England sit atop the 2026 World Cup winner market with probabilities tightly clustered between 11% and 17%, reflecting the depth of elite European squads and recent international results. France benefits from a core of experienced attackers and defensive organization, while Spain\u2019s fluid possession game and emerging talent pool sustain strong trader support. England\u2019s attacking options and tournament experience contribute to its position. Portugal, Germany, the Netherlands, and Argentina remain within striking distance, underscoring the parity across top nations with proven track records in major competitions. The bunched pricing captures the inherent unpredictability of a 32-team field where form, injuries, and matchups can shift outcomes rapidly."
